<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Universal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Universal of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-rada">Central Rada</a>, issued in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> on 20 November 1917 after the Bolshevik seizure of power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a>, proclaimed the Ukrainian People's Republic. It declared the new republic part of a future federal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> rather than independent, and announced land reform, an eight-hour working day and the abolition of the death penalty. It was superseded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-universal">Fourth Universal</a> of January 1918, which declared full independence.</p></div>
